# Entity Framework Core Audit

## Tổng quan

Entity Framework Core Audit là skill chuyên biệt để audit và optimize EF Core implementations. Skill này cung cấp systematic approach để analyze DbContext configurations, identify N+1 query problems, optimize tracking behavior, review relationships, và ensure efficient database operations. Essential cho applications sử dụng EF Core as their ORM.

## Purpose (Mục đử)

EF Core is powerful nhưng easy to misuse:

1. **N+1 queries**: Loading related data inefficiently
2. **Excessive tracking**: Unnecessary change tracking overhead
3. **Missing indexes**: Foreign keys without indexes
4. **Poor projections**: Selecting all columns when not needed
5. **Inefficient queries**: Client-side evaluation, missing eager loading

Entity Framework Core Audit tồn tại để:

- **Identify performance bottlenecks** trong EF Core usage
- **Detect N+1 patterns** before they hit production
- **Optimize tracking behavior** cho different scenarios
- **Review entity relationships** cho efficiency
- **Provide query optimization** recommendations

## Input (Đầu vào)

| Input | Mô tả | Required |
|-------|-------|----------|
| `dbcontext` | DbContext implementation | Yes |
| `entities` | Entity class definitions | Yes |
| `repositories` | Repository patterns used | No |
| `query_logs` | EF Core query logs | No |

## Output (Đầu ra)

| Output | Mô tả | Format |
|--------|-------|--------|
| `n_plus_one_report` | N+1 detection results | Report |
| `tracking_analysis` | Tracking behavior analysis | Analysis |
| `index_recommendations` | Database index suggestions | List |
| `query_optimizations` | Query rewrite suggestions | List |
| `migration_scripts` | DDL for changes | Scripts |

## Workflow (Quy trình)

### Bước 1: DbContext Analysis

```typescript
// Analyze DbContext configuration
interface DbContextAnalysis {
  entities: EntityInfo[];
  relationships: RelationshipInfo[];
  configuration: DbContextConfig;
  issues: ConfigurationIssue[];
}

async function analyzeDbContext(
  dbContextPath: string
): Promise<DbContextAnalysis> {
  const content = await readFile(dbContextPath);
  const parsed = parseDbContext(content);
  
  return {
    entities: extractEntities(parsed),
    relationships: extractRelationships(parsed),
    configuration: analyzeConfiguration(parsed),
    issues: identifyIssues(parsed)
  };
}

function extractEntities(parsed: ParsedDbContext): EntityInfo[] {
  return parsed.entitySets.map(set => ({
    name: set.name,
    entityType: set.entityType,
    tableName: set.tableName || set.name,
    keys: set.keys,
    properties: set.properties.map(p => ({
      name: p.name,
      type: p.clrType,
      columnName: p.columnName,
      isNullable: p.isNullable,
      isRequired: p.isRequired,
      isKey: p.isKey,
      isForeignKey: p.isForeignKey,
      isConcurrencyToken: p.isConcurrencyToken
    })),
    indexes: set.indexes
  }));
}

function extractRelationships(parsed: ParsedDbContext): RelationshipInfo[] {
  return parsed.relationships.map(rel => ({
    name: rel.name,
    entityType: rel.entityType,
    targetEntity: rel.targetEntity,
    type: rel.type, // one-to-one, one-to-many, many-to-many
    foreignKey: rel.foreignKey,
    isRequired: rel.isRequired,
    deleteBehavior: rel.deleteBehavior,
    navigationProperty: rel.navigationProperty,
    inverseNavigation: rel.inverseNavigation
  }));
}
```

### Bước 2: N+1 Query Detection

```typescript
// Detect N+1 query patterns
interface NPlusOneDetection {
  patterns: NPlusOnePattern[];
  locations: NPlusOneLocation[];
  severity: 'critical' | 'high' | 'medium' | 'low';
  totalQueries: number;
  suggestedFixes: FixSuggestion[];
}

class NPlusOneDetector {
  private dbContextPath: string;
  
  constructor(dbContextPath: string) {
    this.dbContextPath = dbContextPath;
  }
  
  async detect(): Promise<NPlusOneDetection> {
    const sourceFiles = await this.findQueryFiles();
    const patterns: NPlusOnePattern[] = [];
    const locations: NPlusOneLocation[] = [];
    
    for (const file of sourceFiles) {
      const content = await readFile(file);
      const tree = parseSyntaxTree(content);
      
      // Check for foreach loops with database access
      const foreachLoops = this.findForeachLoops(tree);
      
      for (const loop of foreachLoops) {
        const queries = this.findQueriesInLoop(loop);
        
        if (queries.length > 0) {
          const pattern = this.classifyPattern(loop, queries);
          patterns.push(pattern);
          
          locations.push({
            file,
            line: loop.startLine,
            method: loop.methodName,
            pattern,
            estimatedQueryCount: this.estimateQueryCount(loop)
          });
        }
      }
      
      // Check for explicit iteration with lazy loading
      const lazyLoads = this.findLazyLoads(tree);
      patterns.push(...lazyLoads.map(l => ({
        type: 'lazy_loading',
        severity: 'high' as const,
        description: 'Lazy loading causes N+1',
        entity: l.entity,
        property: l.property
      })));
      
      // Check for Select N+1 (selecting navigation properties in loop)
      const selectNPlusOne = this.findSelectNPlusOne(tree);
      patterns.push(...selectNPlusOne);
    }
    
    return {
      patterns,
      locations,
      severity: this.calculateOverallSeverity(patterns),
      totalQueries: locations.reduce((sum, l) => sum + l.estimatedQueryCount, 0),
      suggestedFixes: this.generateFixes(patterns)
    };
  }
  
  private findForeachLoops(tree: SyntaxTree): ForeachLoop[] {
    const loops: ForeachLoop[] = [];
    
    // Find all foreach statements
    const foreachStmts = tree.findAll('ForEachStatement');
    
    for (const stmt of foreachStmts) {
      const body = stmt.body;
      
      // Check if body contains database queries
      const queries = this.findQueriesInNode(body);
      
      if (queries.length > 0) {
        loops.push({
          variable: stmt.variable,
          collection: stmt.collection,
          body: body,
          startLine: stmt.startLine,
          endLine: stmt.endLine,
          queries
        });
      }
    }
    
    return loops;
  }
  
  private findQueriesInLoop(loop: ForeachLoop): QueryInfo[] {
    const queries: QueryInfo[] = [];
    
    // Find LINQ queries in loop body
    const methodCalls = loop.body.findAll('InvocationExpression');
    
    for (const call of methodCalls) {
      if (this.isDbSetMethod(call)) {
        queries.push({
          type: this.classifyDbCall(call),
          method: call.methodName,
          line: call.startLine
        });
      }
    }
    
    return queries;
  }
  
  private classifyPattern(
    loop: ForeachLoop,
    queries: QueryInfo[]
  ): NPlusOnePattern {
    // Classic N+1: foreach + query in body
    if (queries.some(q => q.type === 'query')) {
      return {
        type: 'classic_n_plus_one',
        severity: 'critical',
        description: `Query executed ${loop.estimatedIterations || 'N'} times`
      };
    }
    
    // Include in foreach
    if (loop.collection.includes('Include')) {
      return {
        type: 'include_in_foreach',
        severity: 'medium',
        description: 'Include inside foreach - consider batch loading'
      };
    }
    
    // Reference access (lazy loading)
    if (queries.some(q => q.type === 'reference_access')) {
      return {
        type: 'lazy_loading',
        severity: 'high',
        description: 'Navigation property access triggers query'
      };
    }
    
    return {
      type: 'unknown',
      severity: 'low',
      description: 'Potential N+1 pattern'
    };
  }
  
  private findLazyLoads(tree: SyntaxTree): LazyLoadInfo[] {
    const lazyLoads: LazyLoadInfo[] = [];
    
    // Pattern: .Entity.Property where Entity is tracked
    const memberAccesses = tree.findAll('MemberAccessExpression');
    
    for (const access of memberAccesses) {
      // Check if accessing a navigation property
      if (this.isNavigationProperty(access)) {
        lazyLoads.push({
          entity: access.expression.toString(),
          property: access.memberName,
          line: access.startLine
        });
      }
    }
    
    return lazyLoads;
  }
  
  private generateFixes(patterns: NPlusOnePattern[]): FixSuggestion[] {
    return patterns.map(pattern => {
      switch (pattern.type) {
        case 'classic_n_plus_one':
          return {
            pattern: pattern.type,
            fix: 'Use Include() with ThenInclude() for eager loading, or batch query',
            example: `// Before (N+1)\nforeach (var order in orders)\n{\n    var customer = db.Customers.Find(order.CustomerId);\n}\n\n// After (Eager loading)\nvar orders = db.Orders.Include(o => o.Customer).ToList();`
          };
        
        case 'lazy_loading':
          return {
            pattern: pattern.type,
            fix: 'Use eager loading (Include) or explicit loading',
            example: `// Before (Lazy loading)\nvar order = db.Orders.First();\nvar customerName = order.Customer.Name; // Triggers query\n\n// After (Eager loading)\nvar order = db.Orders.Include(o => o.Customer).First();`
          };
        
        case 'collection_in_foreach':
          return {
            pattern: pattern.type,
            fix: 'Use projection or batch query',
            example: `// Before (Collection access)\nforeach (var user in users)\n{\n    var roles = db.Roles.Where(r => r.UserId == user.Id).ToList();\n}\n\n// After (Batch query)\nvar userIds = users.Select(u => u.Id).ToList();\nvar rolesByUser = db.Roles.Where(r => userIds.Contains(r.UserId)).ToLookup(r => r.UserId);`
          };
        
        default:
          return {
            pattern: pattern.type,
            fix: 'Review query pattern',
            example: ''
          };
      }
    });
  }
}
```

### Bước 3: Tracking Behavior Analysis

```typescript
// Analyze tracking behavior
interface TrackingAnalysis {
  queries: QueryTrackingInfo[];
  issues: TrackingIssue[];
  recommendations: TrackingRecommendation[];
}

async function analyzeTracking(
  dbContext: string,
  repositories: string[]
): Promise<TrackingAnalysis> {
  const queries: QueryTrackingInfo[] = [];
  const issues: TrackingIssue[] = [];
  
  // Analyze DbContext configuration
  const content = await readFile(dbContext);
  const queriesInContext = findAllQueries(content);
  
  for (const query of queriesInContext) {
    const trackingInfo = analyzeQueryTracking(query);
    queries.push(trackingInfo);
    
    // Check for unnecessary tracking
    if (trackingInfo.isTracked && !trackingInfo.modifiesData) {
      issues.push({
        type: 'unnecessary_tracking',
        query: trackingInfo.query,
        severity: 'medium',
        suggestion: 'Add .AsNoTracking() for read-only queries',
        impact: 'Memory usage and change tracking overhead'
      });
    }
    
    // Check for tracking with projections
    if (trackingInfo.isTracked && trackingInfo.hasProjection) {
      issues.push({
        type: 'tracking_with_projection',
        query: trackingInfo.query,
        severity: 'low',
        suggestion: 'Use AsNoTracking() with projections for better performance',
        impact: 'Unnecessary entity materialization'
      });
    }
  }
  
  // Check repository patterns
  for (const repo of repositories) {
    const repoContent = await readFile(repo);
    const repoQueries = findAllQueries(repoContent);
    
    for (const query of repoQueries) {
      // Read operations should typically use AsNoTracking
      if (isReadOnlyQuery(query) && !query.asNoTracking) {
        issues.push({
          type: 'tracking_in_read',
          query: query.query,
          location: repo,
          severity: 'medium',
          suggestion: 'Use AsNoTracking() for read-only operations'
        });
      }
    }
  }
  
  return {
    queries,
    issues,
    recommendations: generateTrackingRecommendations(issues)
  };
}

function analyzeQueryTracking(query: ParsedQuery): QueryTrackingInfo {
  return {
    query: query.raw,
    isTracked: !query.asNoTracking && !query.asNoTrackingWithIdentityResolution,
    hasProjection: query.selectClause !== null,
    modifiesData: false, // Would need more analysis
    usesInclude: query.includes.length > 0,
    usesThenInclude: query.thenIncludes.length > 0,
    useOfSplitQuery: query.isSplitQuery
  };
}
```

### Bước 4: Index Recommendations

```typescript
// Generate index recommendations
interface IndexRecommendation {
  table: string;
  columns: string[];
  indexType: 'btree' | 'hash' | 'gin' | 'gist';
  reason: string;
  estimatedImpact: string;
  existingIndex?: string;
  migration: string;
}

async function generateIndexRecommendations(
  dbContextPath: string
): Promise<IndexRecommendation[]> {
  const recommendations: IndexRecommendation[] = [];
  
  // Analyze foreign keys
  const relationships = await extractRelationships(dbContextPath);
  
  for (const rel of relationships) {
    // Check if FK column has index
    const hasIndex = await checkIndexExists(rel.tableName, rel.foreignKeyColumns);
    
    if (!hasIndex) {
      recommendations.push({
        table: rel.tableName,
        columns: rel.foreignKeyColumns,
        indexType: 'btree',
        reason: 'Foreign key column should be indexed for join performance',
        estimatedImpact: `Improves ${rel.type} query performance`,
        migration: `CREATE INDEX idx_${rel.tableName}_${rel.foreignKeyColumns.join('_')} ON ${rel.tableName} (${rel.foreignKeyColumns.join(', ')});`
      });
    }
  }
  
  // Analyze WHERE clauses
  const queries = await extractWhereClauses(dbContextPath);
  const columnUsage = countColumnUsageInWhere(queries);
  
  for (const [table, columns] of Object.entries(columnUsage)) {
    for (const [column, count] of Object.entries(columns)) {
      if (count >= 3) { // Column used in 3+ WHERE clauses
        const hasIndex = await checkIndexExists(table, [column]);
        
        if (!hasIndex) {
          recommendations.push({
            table,
            columns: [column],
            indexType: 'btree',
            reason: `Column used in ${count} WHERE clauses`,
            estimatedImpact: 'High - frequently filtered column',
            migration: `CREATE INDEX idx_${table}_${column} ON ${table} (${column});`
          });
        }
      }
    }
  }
  
  // Analyze ORDER BY clauses
  const orderByColumns = await extractOrderByColumns(dbContextPath);
  
  for (const [table, columns] of Object.entries(orderByColumns)) {
    if (columns.length > 0) {
      const existingIndex = await findCoveringIndex(table, columns);
      
      if (!existingIndex) {
        recommendations.push({
          table,
          columns,
          indexType: 'btree',
          reason: 'Columns used in ORDER BY',
          estimatedImpact: 'Eliminates sort operations',
          migration: `CREATE INDEX idx_${table}_${columns.join('_')} ON ${table} (${columns.join(', ')});`
        });
      }
    }
  }
  
  return recommendations;
}

function countColumnUsageInWhere(
  queries: ParsedQuery[]
): Record<string, Record<string, number>> {
  const usage: Record<string, Record<string, number>> = {};
  
  for (const query of queries) {
    for (const column of query.filteredColumns) {
      if (!usage[column.table]) {
        usage[column.table] = {};
      }
      usage[column.table][column.name] = (usage[column.table][column.name] || 0) + 1;
    }
  }
  
  return usage;
}
```

### Bước 5: Query Optimization

```typescript
// Generate query optimization suggestions
interface QueryOptimization {
  original: string;
  optimized: string;
  technique: string;
  estimatedImprovement: string;
  beforeMetrics: QueryMetrics;
  afterMetrics: QueryMetrics;
}

class QueryOptimizer {
  async optimizeQueries(
    slowQueries: ParsedQuery[]
  ): Promise<QueryOptimization[]> {
    const optimizations: QueryOptimization[] = [];
    
    for (const query of slowQueries) {
      const optimization = await this.optimizeQuery(query);
      if (optimization) {
        optimizations.push(optimization);
      }
    }
    
    return optimizations;
  }
  
  private async optimizeQuery(query: ParsedQuery): Promise<QueryOptimization | null> {
    const techniques: OptimizationTechnique[] = [];
    
    // Check for SELECT *
    if (query.hasSelectStar) {
      techniques.push({
        name: 'Projection',
        description: 'Select only needed columns',
        example: `// Before\nvar data = db.Products.ToList();\n\n// After\nvar data = db.Products\n    .Select(p => new { p.Id, p.Name, p.Price })\n    .ToList();`
      });
    }
    
    // Check for missing AsNoTracking
    if (!query.asNoTracking && isReadOnly(query)) {
      techniques.push({
        name: 'NoTracking',
        description: 'Disable change tracking for read-only queries',
        example: `db.Products.AsNoTracking().Where(...).ToList();`
      });
    }
    
    // Check for client-side evaluation
    if (query.hasClientEvaluation) {
      techniques.push({
        name: 'ServerSideEvaluation',
        description: 'Move filtering to database',
        example: `// Avoid client-side evaluation\ndb.Products.Where(p => ExpensiveMethod(p)).ToList();\n\n// Use server-side filtering\ndb.Products.Where(p => p.Price > minPrice).ToList();`
      });
    }
    
    // Check for missing pagination
    if (!query.hasSkipTake && query.mayReturnMany) {
      techniques.push({
        name: 'Pagination',
        description: 'Add pagination to limit result size',
        example: `db.Products.Skip(0).Take(pageSize).ToList();`
      });
    }
    
    // Generate optimized query
    let optimized = query.raw;
    
    for (const tech of techniques) {
      optimized = this.applyOptimization(optimized, tech.name);
    }
    
    if (techniques.length === 0) {
      return null;
    }
    
    return {
      original: query.raw,
      optimized,
      technique: techniques.map(t => t.name).join(', '),
      estimatedImprovement: this.estimateImprovement(techniques),
      beforeMetrics: await this.measureQuery(query.raw),
      afterMetrics: await this.measureQuery(optimized)
    };
  }
  
  private applyOptimization(query: string, technique: string): string {
    // Simplified - actual implementation would be more sophisticated
    switch (technique) {
      case 'NoTracking':
        if (!query.includes('AsNoTracking')) {
          const match = query.match(/(\w+)\.(\w+)\(/);
          if (match) {
            return query.replace(
              match[0],
              `${match[1]}.${match[2]}.AsNoTracking(`
            );
          }
        }
        return query;
        
      case 'Pagination':
        if (!query.includes('Skip') && !query.includes('Take')) {
          return query.replace('ToList()', 'Take(1000).ToList()');
        }
        return query;
        
      default:
        return query;
    }
  }
}
```

### Bước 6: Migration Planning

```typescript
// Generate migration scripts
interface MigrationPlan {
  indexMigrations: string[];
  queryChanges: QueryChange[];
  breakingChanges: BreakingChange[];
  rollbackPlan: string;
}

function generateMigrationPlan(
  recommendations: {
    indexes: IndexRecommendation[];
    queryOptimizations: QueryOptimization[];
    trackingChanges: TrackingIssue[];
  }
): MigrationPlan {
  const indexMigrations: string[] = [];
  const queryChanges: QueryChange[] = [];
  const breakingChanges: BreakingChange[] = [];
  
  // Index migrations
  for (const idx of recommendations.indexes) {
    indexMigrations.push(`-- Create index for ${idx.table}.${idx.columns.join(', ')}
CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY IF NOT EXISTS idx_${idx.table}_${idx.columns.join('_')}
ON ${idx.table} (${idx.columns.join(', ')});`);
  }
  
  // Query changes
  for (const opt of recommendations.queryOptimizations) {
    queryChanges.push({
      file: opt.sourceFile,
      original: opt.original,
      optimized: opt.optimized,
      reason: opt.technique
    });
  }
  
  return {
    indexMigrations,
    queryChanges,
    breakingChanges,
    rollbackPlan: generateRollbackPlan(recommendations)
  };
}
```

## Checklist (Danh sách kiểm tra)

- [ ] All foreign keys have indexes
- [ ] Read-only queries use AsNoTracking()
- [ ] Eager loading (Include) used instead of lazy loading
- [ ] No SELECT * in queries
- [ ] Pagination on all list endpoints
- [ ] No N+1 patterns in loops
- [ ] Split queries for large collections
- [ ] Proper use of AsNoTrackingWithIdentityResolution
- [ ] Batch operations for bulk updates
- [ ] Change tracking disabled where appropriate
- [ ] No client-side evaluation
- [ ] Compiled queries for repeated operations
- [ ] Global query filters for soft deletes
- [ ] Proper concurrency tokens configured
- [ ] Indexes for frequently filtered columns

