### Ví dụ 2: Fix N+1 Pattern

```typescript
// Common N+1 pattern detection và fix

// ❌ BEFORE: N+1 Query
async function GetOrdersWithCustomers_N_plus_1(orderIds: number[]) {
  var orders = await _context.Orders
    .Where(o => orderIds.Contains(o.Id))
    .ToListAsync();
  
  var result = new List<OrderDto>();
  foreach (var order in orders) {
    // N+1: Query for each customer!
    var customer = await _context.Customers.FindAsync(order.CustomerId);
    result.Add(new OrderDto {
      OrderId = order.Id,
      CustomerName = customer.Name
    });
  }
  return result;
}

// ✅ AFTER: Eager Loading
async function GetOrdersWithCustomers_Eager(orderIds: number[]) {
  var orders = await _context.Orders
    .Where(o => orderIds.Contains(o.Id))
    .Include(o => o.Customer)  // Eager load
    .AsNoTracking()  // Read-only
    .ToListAsync();
  
  return orders.Select(o => new OrderDto {
    OrderId = o.Id,
    CustomerName = o.Customer.Name
  }).ToList();
}

// ✅ ALTERNATIVE: Projection
async function GetOrdersWithCustomers_Projection(orderIds: number[]) {
  return await _context.Orders
    .Where(o => orderIds.Contains(o.Id))
    .Select(o => new OrderDto {
      OrderId = o.Id,
      CustomerName = o.Customer.Name  // EF handles this efficiently
    })
    .AsNoTracking()
    .ToListAsync();
}
```

## Anti Patterns (Các pattern cần tránh)

### 1. Lazy Loading Everywhere
```csharp
// ❌ BAD: Lazy loading enabled globally
protected override void OnConfiguring(DbContextOptionsBuilder options)
    => options.UseLazyLoadingProxies();

// ❌ BAD: Accessing navigation in loop
foreach (var order in orders)
{
    var customerName = order.Customer.Name; // Triggers query each time!
}

// ✅ GOOD: Eager loading
var orders = await _context.Orders
    .Include(o => o.Customer)
    .AsNoTracking()
    .ToListAsync();
```

### 2. Tracking Everything
```csharp
// ❌ BAD: Track all queries
var products = await _context.Products.ToListAsync();

// ✅ GOOD: No tracking for read-only
var products = await _context.Products
    .AsNoTracking()
    .ToListAsync();
```

### 3. SELECT * Usage
```csharp
// ❌ BAD: Select all columns
var products = await _context.Products.ToListAsync();

// ✅ GOOD: Select only needed columns
var products = await _context.Products
    .Select(p => new { p.Id, p.Name, p.Price })
    .AsNoTracking()
    .ToListAsync();
```

### 4. Missing Pagination
```csharp
// ❌ BAD: Load all records
var orders = await _context.Orders.ToListAsync(); // Could be millions!

// ✅ GOOD: Paginate
var orders = await _context.Orders
    .OrderBy(o => o.OrderDate)
    .Skip(page * pageSize)
    .Take(pageSize)
    .AsNoTracking()
    .ToListAsync();
```

### 5. Synchronous Over Async
```csharp
// ❌ BAD: Synchronous call
var order = _context.Orders.FirstOrDefault(o => o.Id == id);

// ✅ GOOD: Async for web applications
var order = await _context.Orders
    .FirstOrDefaultAsync(o => o.Id == id);
```

## Best Practices (Thực hành tốt nhất)

1. **Disable lazy loading by default**: Enable only when needed explicitly
2. **Use AsNoTracking() for read-only queries**: Significant performance gain
3. **Use Include() for related data**: Batch load instead of lazy loading
4. **Project to DTOs**: Select only needed data
5. **Paginate list endpoints**: Always limit result sets
6. **Use compiled queries for hot paths**: Repeated similar queries
7. **Configure indexes in Fluent API**: Document expected queries
8. **Use split queries for large Include()**: Avoid Cartesian product
9. **Consider stored procedures for complex queries**: When EF can't optimize
10. **Monitor query performance**: Use logging and profiling

